 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Keep it simple. Start with everyone seated, then bring in the cake or bread and cut the first piece together. You can each choose a short story or memoir that ties into the day, like adventure, hope or friendship. Or one person tells short story without looking at the box. Yes, a shared meal beforehand ritual. Make it about the couple, not a deity. Things like lighting candles, drinking from single glass or toasting with the wedding ring feel ritual without being religious. Lovely. A small pot of sweetcorn or sunflowers growing up the side of the path works. Plant it in the garden at home too, so it has a proper home to go after the ceremony.",
